#service
act as loand balance and connection between the pods
consider i have pod for front end, back end and database (three pods)
so the service has to know the request for which pod
Service yml file have the selector: label so according to the lable it connnect with pods
but pod ip required to send the request to pod
while creating the service simoultaneously it create endpoint
endpoint will give the all pod ip

#kube-proxy
it will available in all nodes
it has two ip one is service ip and endpoints
if request is sent to service it firs goes to kube-proxy, it will check in table which service has received the request
kube proxy has to decide to which endpoint ip need to share the load
it will use round robin algorithm to share the load
kube-proxy will forward the request to endpoint ip
#pod
pod is the smallest deployable unit in kubernets
pod can have one or more containers inside it
pod can have shared storage and network
pod can have specification how to run the container
pod can have labels and name
pod can have resource limit and request
pod can have restart policy like always, on failure, never
pod can have node selector to run the pod in specific node
pod can have affinity and anti affinity to run the pod in specific node or not to run the
pod in specific node
pod can have toleration to run the pod in specific node which has taint
pod can have init container to run the container before the main container
pod can have liveness probe to check the health of the container
pod can have readiness probe to check the container is ready to accept the request
pod can have startup probe to check the container is started or not
pod can have security context to define the security of the pod or container
pod can have image pull secret to pull the image from private registry
pod can have resource limit and request to define the resource for the container
pod can have env to define the environment variable for the container
pod can have config map to define the configuration for the container
pod can have secret to define the secret for the container
pod can have volume to define the storage for the container
pod can have volume mount to mount the storage for the container
pod can have host path to mount the host path for the container
pod can have empty dir to create empty directory for the container
pod can have downward api to get the pod information for the container
pod can have projected volume to combine multiple volume for the container
pod can have CSI volume to use the CSI driver for the container
pod can have ephemeral volume to create temporary volume for the container
pod can have resource limit and request to define the resource for the container
